<title>INDIA: India ACC 96/97 1st half net down 56 pct.</title>
<headline>India ACC 96/97 1st half net down 56 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    550.5 vs   1,255.7</p>
<p>    Net sales	  12,214.6 vs  11,163.9</p>
<p>    Other income	  202.3 vs     109.3</p>
<p>    Expenditure	10,611.1 vs   9,258.3</p>
<p>    Interest costs	546.6 vs     423.9</p>
<p>    Depreciation	  367.3 vs     283.7</p>
<p>    Taxation		313.0 vs     343.0</p>
<p>    Div from UTI units   70.5 vs     133.1</p>
<p>    Profit on sale of    nil  vs     204.3</p>
<p>Investments</p>
<p>    Sales tax liability  98.9 vs     nil</p>
<p>    Receipt against ACC  nil  vs	20.4</p>
<p>Babcock dues</p>
<p>    Employee bonus	 nil  vs	66.4</p>
<p>Note: Associated Cement Companies (ACC) -- India's largest cement maker -- said cement output during the six months to September rose to 4.57 million tonnes from 4.4 million a year ago. Cement sales rose to 4.43 million tonnes from 4.3 million.</p>
<p>ACC said it could not recover an unprecedented increase in input cost, affecting margins.</p>
<p>--  Bombay newsroom (91-22-265 9000)</p>
</text>
